std.string — Low-level string operations
==========================================

Primitive string functions backed by the host runtime.
For higher-level utilities see `std.strings`.

    module std.string


Functions
---------

### length

Return the character count of a string.

    extern length(s: string) -> int

### concat

Concatenate two strings.

    extern concat(a: string, b: string) -> string

### substr

Return a substring starting at `start` with the given `length`.

    extern substr(s: string, start: int, length: int) -> string

### index_of

Return the index of the first occurrence of `needle` in `s`, or -1.

    extern index_of(s: string, needle: string) -> int

### starts_with

Check whether `s` starts with `prefix`.

    extern starts_with(s: string, prefix: string) -> bool

### ends_with

Check whether `s` ends with `suffix`.

    extern ends_with(s: string, suffix: string) -> bool

### trim

Remove leading and trailing whitespace.

    extern trim(s: string) -> string

### split

Split a string by a delimiter.

    extern split(s: string, sep: string) -> []string

### to_int

Parse a string as a 64-bit integer.

    extern to_int(s: string) -> i64

### from_int

Convert a 64-bit integer to its string representation.

    extern from_int(n: i64) -> string

### char_at

Return the character code at index `i`.

    extern char_at(s: string, i: int) -> int

### equal

Check whether two strings are equal.

    extern equal(a: string, b: string) -> bool

### contains

Check whether `s` contains `needle`.

    extern contains(s: string, needle: string) -> bool
